# The five dashboard views need no keys.
# "Ask the data" calls models through Vercel AI Gateway (AI SDK). Copy to .env.local, never commit values.
#
# Auth to the gateway:
#   - On Vercel: automatic. The deployment gets VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN, so no key is stored in project env vars.
#   - Locally: either an API key ...
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
#   ... or run `vercel link` then `vercel env pull` to write a short-lived VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN to .env.local.
#
# Which model answers. Any "provider/model" id from https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1/models.
# Unset = openai/gpt-6-luna.
ASK_MODEL=
#
# LOCAL EVAL ONLY (pipeline/eval_ask.mjs). Lets the request body pick the model and drop the
# prompt's write rule. Leave unset everywhere else, and never set it on a deployment.
# ASK_ALLOW_MODEL_OVERRIDE=1
#
# Zero data retention + no prompt training are requested on every model call (fail closed).
# ZDR needs a Pro or Enterprise team: on a Hobby-plan key the gateway answers 403, so set ASK_ZDR=0
# for local work on such a key. Never set it to 0 on a deployment.
# ASK_ZDR=0
#
# Shows the model switch in the Ask panel (the three allowlisted models in lib/askModels.json).
# The server ignores any model not on the allowlist. Set on Vercel by the owner for the demo.
# ASK_DEMO_MODEL_SWITCH=1
